WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.968
We are following breaking news

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.536
out of Japan this morning.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:07.507
A powerful earthquake measuring 7.5

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.409
has triggered evacuations

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.077
and a tsunami warning.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.679
You're looking at the moment

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.680
the quake struck.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.148
Video from along the coast.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.584
There you can see the shaking.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.219
It went on for some time.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.820
Here is more video

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.056
from the Ishikawa Prefecture in Japan.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:23.790
The population

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.991
there is about a million people.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:25.291
This is

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.394
on the western coast of Japan,

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.996
about 185 miles from Tokyo.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.297
Again, from this footage,

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:31.631
you can see

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:35.168
just how long this shaking went on for.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.137
You can see the poles there on the left

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.605
starting to sway.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.239
Ultimately,

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.841
this did lead to some building collapses.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.978
And shortly you'll see dust rising

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.013
from the collapsed building there

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.715
on the left side of your screen.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.084
Again, very powerful shaking

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.486
felt by millions of people,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.189
about a million people or so

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.525
in the more severe area

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.326
where this earthquake struck.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.261
Japanese officials

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.529
have now lowered

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.596
their tsunami alert

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.231
from a major tsunami warning.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.201
It is now a tsunami warning, period.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.204
They could expect waves of up to ten

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.439
feet there.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.740
And the aftershocks there

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.775
warning could last days.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.976
We are getting new video

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.845
from inside a parking garage

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.046
you can see here

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:23.516
these cars just shaking there inside this

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.351
this solid structure.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.587
Again, you get a sense of the power

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.056
of this earthquake.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.524
We have team coverage this morning.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:31.991
Derek Van

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.660
Dam is tracking the tsunami threat.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.094
We're going to start

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.061
with Hanako Montgomery,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.596
who is live in Tokyo.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.764
Give us the latest from there.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.169
Yeah, good morning, John.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.637
So right now, as you mentioned,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.473
the tsunami warning has been lowered.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.341
We're still expecting to see

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.843
ten feet of waves, though.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.112
So still very, very frightening

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:52.712
and daunting

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.446
for many people

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.682
living in Ishikawa Prefecture.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.517
Just to note some of the damage

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.918
that we've been seeing.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.519
At least.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.955
33,000 homes have lost power.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.657
Others have collapsed.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.092
We're seeing reports of people

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.328
being trapped under their homes.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.062
As well.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.931
We're also knowing that about a thousand

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.233
self-defense force

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.934
personnel have been dispatched

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.136
and they're trying to confirm

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.004
any of the survivors

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.539
in Ishikawa Prefecture.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.142
We also know that 20 self-defense force

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.411
planes and also other vessels

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.746
are trying to confirm

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.781
just the extent of this damage.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.351
So this powerful, powerful earthquake,

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:31.651
you know,

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.219
was also a shallow earthquake,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.821
which is very significant to note,

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.756
because with shallow earthquakes,

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.892
they can actually trigger very powerful

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.393
and destructive tsunamis,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.828
even though the tsunami level

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.096
has been dropped down

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.397
to just a tsunami warning,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.400
we are still expecting to see large waves

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.668
coming out of the western

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.337
part of Japan, John Hanako

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.739
I think everyone in everyone's

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.239
memories are

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.141
what happened in 2011 in Japan

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.509
with the powerful earthquake there

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.877
and the destruction of the Fukushima

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.546
nuclear power plant.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.114
Any concerns this morning

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.916
as the morning or the evening develops

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.917
in Japan

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.652
about things like that, power

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.953
plants and nuclear power

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:11.858
Yeah, John.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.859
So we're

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.561
getting information from the

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.929
from the Japanese government

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.864
that there are currently

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.532
no nuclear abnormalities

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.633
at any of the nuclear

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.036
power plants close to the epicenter

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.737
near Ishikawa Prefecture.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.306
However, of course, this moment,

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:26.973
this terrible,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.274
terrible moment

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.277
in Japanese history, the 2011 earthquake

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.679
and tsunami is very present

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.681
in many people's minds.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.616
Today is New Year's Day here in Japan,

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.151
when many people are celebrating

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.219
with their families,

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.853
with their friends at home,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.454
and suddenly

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.889
their TVs are telling them

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.791
to evacuate to get to higher ground.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.359
And just a very frightening moment

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.628
for many people in the country,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:51.030
specifically on western Japan, that coast

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.131
where you actually don't

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:52.966
historically see

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.568
very many earthquakes of this size.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:56.336
So, again,

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.537
just a lot of

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.938
scared feelings

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.540
and just a lot of tension right now

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.508
to see what kind of damage

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.143
this subsequent tsunami

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.279
could bring to western Japan. John.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.481
Frayed nerves in the region, to be sure.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.149
Hanako Montgomery, keep us posted

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.051
throughout the rest of the morning.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:12.185
Well,

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.286
this now is meteorologist

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:13.987
Derek Van Dam,

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:16.155
who was following the tsunami threat.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.590
Derek, what are you seeing?

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.091
Yeah, well,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.358
I mean,

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.460
just seeing video of this stirs

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.262
up emotions from 2011

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.963
when I covered the tsunami

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.633
that reached the East Coast of Japan.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:29.168
But this is some of the latest video of

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.536
the tsunami wave

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.805
that reached the western shorelines

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.575
of the Honshu Honshu region.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.376
So we're

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.443
looking at

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.478
a tsunami wave

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.179
traveling up to Saiki River

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.881
in a town called Jitsu.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.882
It's got a population

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.817
of about 200,000 people

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.054
and this wave height that we're seeing,

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.155
this is some new video

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.456
so we're getting it as it comes.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.959
Telling you and analyzing it in real time

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.193
really fits the narrative

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.495
of some of the observed

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.562
